---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Crisis Resources & Hotlines | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Hotlines, national databases, and domestic violence resources for families of missing persons and homicide victims — plus internet safety guidance."
  heading="Resources & hotlines"
  intro="Help that's available right now, from organizations we trust."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Get help', href: '/get-help' },
    { label: 'Resources & hotlines', href: '/get-help/resources' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <h2>Immediate help</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> call <a href="tel:911">911</a></li>
      <li><strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline:</strong> call <a href="tel:18007997233">1-800-799-7233</a>, text START to 88788, or chat at <a href="https://www.thehotline.org/" rel="noopener">thehotline.org</a></li>
      <li><strong>Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline:</strong> call or text <a href="tel:988">988</a></li>
      <li><strong>National Sexual Assault Hotline (RAINN):</strong> <a href="tel:18006564673">1-800-656-4673</a></li>
      <li><strong>NCMEC (missing children):</strong> <a href="tel:18008435678">1-800-843-5678</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Missing &amp; unidentified persons databases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://namus.nij.ojp.gov/" rel="noopener"><strong>NamUs</strong></a> — the national database for missing, unidentified, and unclaimed persons. If your loved one is missing, a complete NamUs profile matters more than almost anything else you can do online.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.missingkids.org/" rel="noopener"><strong>NCMEC</strong></a> — the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children.</li>
      <li><a href="https://charleyproject.org/" rel="noopener"><strong>The Charley Project</strong></a> — detailed profiles of long-term missing person cases.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.doenetwork.org/" rel="noopener"><strong>The Doe Network</strong></a> — volunteer-driven database of missing and unidentified persons.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.in.gov/isp/" rel="noopener"><strong>Indiana State Police</strong></a> — including the Indiana Missing Persons bulletin.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Not sure how these fit together? Our
      <a href="/programs/missing-persons">missing persons program</a> helps
      families get cases entered and reconciled across all of them, free.
    </p>

    <h2 id="internet-safety">Internet safety note</h2>
    <p>
      If you live with someone who hurts or controls you, assume they may be
      able to see your browsing history, your phone, or both.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The <strong>Quick exit</strong> button (bottom corner of every page, or press Escape twice) immediately replaces this site with a neutral page.</li>
      <li>Quick exit cannot erase your history. When you can, browse from a library computer, a work device, or a trusted friend's phone instead.</li>
      <li>Private/incognito windows don't sync history, but they don't hide your activity from monitoring apps already installed on the device.</li>
      <li>The National DV Hotline's <a href="https://www.thehotline.org/plan-for-safety/internet-safety/" rel="noopener">internet safety guide</a> covers this in depth.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>For grief and trauma support</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>National Organization of Parents of Murdered Children:</strong> <a href="https://pomc.org/" rel="noopener">pomc.org</a></li>
      <li><strong>GriefShare</strong> support groups: <a href="https://www.griefshare.org/" rel="noopener">griefshare.org</a></li>
      <li>Our <a href="/programs/outreach-advocacy">outreach &amp; advocacy program</a> can connect you with local, in-person support.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
